  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Formation without product cloning",
      "items": [
        "Greenfield: inspect the founding state and expected absence, then preview a minimal native scaffold through Skills. Preserve customization and upgrade provenance from first generation; first acceptance uses the same local protocol.",
        "ETHOS plans the tracked .ethos/profile.toml binding. A differing nonempty binding is a conflict: no implicit merge, overlay, alias or migration. Existing unrelated files stay outside adoption scope.",
        "Optional capabilities retain their owners: Skills and generators prepare native assets; OpenSpec owns its carrier; docs, skill governance and provider tools own their projections. A profile points at native roots without imposing ETHOS product layout, branch names or provider configuration."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Admission and result are different claims",
      "items": [
        "All required inputs: Authorized subject; Applicable authority; Compiled Commitment; Fresh observations; TransitionPlan; Integrated candidate; Local executed claim.",
        "Required claim selector: all declared proof-plane claims whose exact subject, predicate, scope, bindings, validity and verifier apply.",
        "Attestation is the sole durable semantic result, scoped by predicate, bindings, validity and verifier, never permission. Commitment, Facts and Plan are transient. Change relations and experiments are derived: no persistent workflow graph, compatibility residue, feedback ledger or memory-backed truth.",
        "Own candidate, policy, fresh authority and proof belong to this repository. Shared admission grammar does not import the ETHOS accepted root, another repository’s objects or its permission."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Refusal and uncertainty are different",
      "items": [
        "A stale effect-time check admits no runner. A definite CAS mismatch means this local CAS did not update its ref; it does not undo earlier effects or other resources. An uncertain outcome must be observed before any further attempt.",
        "Contradiction or missing meaning blocks the affected effect. Preserve the counterexample, promote the smallest model boundary and recompile; no exception route around authority."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Binding is not permission or historical approval",
      "items": [
        "Preview is reviewable and idempotent; adoption is reversible before first governed effect. Retain customization and upgrade provenance. No retroactive approval is conferred on inherited history.",
        "The present binding command requires explicit authorization and exact HEAD. Terminal mutation-capable adoption additionally initializes and verifies official OpenSpec; without that carrier, a repository remains observation-only. The explanatory preparation path does not claim that every terminal behavior is implemented today.",
        "A first effect still binds current subject, policy, intent, Facts, Plan, exact object and applicable proof. Missing facts, conflicts or stale state block it. Neither successful scaffold generation nor an installed profile grants a reusable PASS."
      ]
    }
  ]
